# GitHub-first H3 optimization execution

- Always follow [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) across this repository.
- GitHub Project and Issues are the live execution source, not a local todo or chat checkpoint.
- Read [issue receipts](../../artifacts/diagnostics/github-execution/issue_receipts.json)
  and [project receipt](../../artifacts/diagnostics/github-execution/project_receipt.json),
  then fetch the roadmap/current Issue, native dependencies, owner, comments and Project fields.
- Before work: verify readiness, assign the actual executor, comment the precise experiment contract,
  update In Progress. A board task never grants compute-resource permission.
- End work: comment baseline/candidate/restored timings with scope, actual kernel/copy evidence,
  numeric and memory results, failure/cleanup receipts and commit/PR; update Project and parent Issue.
- Use Keep / Reject / Awaiting approval. Reject can complete an experiment but never adopts it.
  A numeric change restores the baseline and requires an explicit user decision; noise is not permission.
- Never close the main roadmap solely because a benchmark, 49-step run or project setup succeeded.
- Preserve original H3/R124+FA, FP16/FP32 exceptions and all155strict checks; **TP remains ON**.
  Current baseline DiT TP2+USP4/encoderTP8 uses all8; topology is two4-card HCCS islands.
- No local weight/activation downloads, BF16/HF32/clipping, teacher hidden cache or student/LoRA.
  Approximate caching, quantization, sparse attention and fewer steps default to not authorized.
- Owned live-claimed hardware only; private changes/IPC; no shared SDK/device reset; release lease.
- If GitHub cannot be read/written, report the blocker and reconcile receipts instead of inventing state.
- [PLAN.md](../../artifacts/diagnostics/github-execution/PLAN.md) records rationale and initial sequencing,
  not live status. R126 commit4384e89 is evidence, not an automatic precision promotion.
